  "hypothesis": "Use one constant bulk/end geometry for the four-vector-remainder class,aligning bulk through an operation-local safe hint. Compared with DCA/DCP,remove per-row division,two-plan selection,and variable tail loop. Always copy one bounded64B head and256B end; accept64extra transferred bytes per row and~24ns hint cost only if complete operations improve. Current byte profile locates memory work,not proof of alignment stalls or gain.",
  "endState": "One small eligible separate-buffer kernel with constant bulk/end,ordinary bounded vector spans and prompt-release hint. Preserve measured alias/vertical/portable kernels. No general alignment cache,pinning framework or fixture-specific state.",
